{"created": "2026-04-24T05:33:41.112186+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-24T05:33:41.547588+00:00", "id": 19723114, "conceptrecid": "17988285", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19723114", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17988285", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19723114", "metadata": {"title": "PCB-IND: Industrial Printed Circuit Board Surface Defect Dataset for Object Detection", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19723114", "publication_date": "2026-04-24", "description": "<p>PCB-IND is an industrial printed circuit board (PCB) surface defect dataset for object detection. The dataset contains&nbsp;<strong>4,789</strong> ROI images collected from a real automated optical inspection (AOI) production line and covers eight defect categories: <strong>mouse_bite, missing_copper, scratch, spurious_copper, copper_burr, stain, short, and open</strong>.</p>\n<p>The dataset is split into<strong> training (3,833 images), validation (478 images), and test (478 images)</strong> subsets. All image patches are provided at a fixed resolution of <strong>300 &times; 300</strong> pixels. Verified annotations are released in YOLO, PASCAL VOC, and MS COCO formats to support different object detection frameworks.</p>\n<p>To improve release consistency and reproducibility, the updated version includes a machine-readable label map file (classes.json) and a revised README file that explicitly documents the official class definitions, dataset organization, and annotation formats. The dataset is primarily intended for AOI candidate verification and patch-level defect detection under real industrial imaging conditions.</p>\n<p>License: CC BY 4.0.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Yan, Hao", "affiliation": "Fujian Polytechnic Normal University"}], "keywords": ["PCB", "defect detection", "YOLO", "COCO", "VOC"], "dates": [{"type": "available"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 3, "